50% - 90% Sparsity):**</span> Contains specific heavy equipment indicators (e.g., `Forks`, `DrivetrainType`, `UtilizationTier`) along with an extensive string of anonymized tracking variables. These columns require robust sentinel missingness encoding (`'Unknown'`) to preserve pattern structures cleanly within gradient boosted tree branches.\n* <span style=\"color:#3498db\">**Blue Zone (<50% Sparsity):**</span> Contains key continuous metrics like `OperationalHoursMeter` (**40.84%** missing). This specific tier is best handled through joint strategic preprocessing: a binary missingness indicator column (`Hours_isna`) combined with a robust median imputation to protect underlying distribution models from tail distortions.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"# Plot 3.4: Median Price by Equipment Classification\ncat_price=(train.groupby('FunctionalClassification')[TARGET]\n             .agg(['median','count'])\n             .query('count >= 200')\n             .sort_values('median')\n             .tail(15))\n\nfig,ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(12, 5))\nfig.suptitle('Plot 3.4: Median Price by Equipment Classification ',fontsize=14,fontweight='bold')\nax.barh(cat_price.index,cat_price['median'], color=sns.color_palette('plasma',len(cat_price)))\nax.set_xlabel(\"Median TargetValue ($)\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-17T09:50:08.247613Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-07-17T09:50:08.248615Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-07-17T09:50:08.514706Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-07-17T09:50:08.248544Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-07-17T09:50:08.513539Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"<Figure size 1200x500 with 1 Axes>","image/png":"\n"},"metadata":{}}],"execution_count":65},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":"### Plot 3.4: Value Hierarchies by Equipment Classification\nAggregating asset prices across high-volume classifications (minimum 200 trades) highlights distinct pricing thresholds determined by functional capacity and heavy equipment dimensions:\n* **The High-End Tier:** Large industrial machinery dominates the maximum distribution peaks. `Motorgrader - 170.0 to 200.0 Horsepower` exhibits the highest valuation threshold with a median asset cost approaching `$91,000`, closely followed by heavy-duty earth-moving assets (`Wheel Loader - 200.0 to 225.0 Horsepower & Track Type Tractor, Dozer - 260.0 + Horsepower`) hovering near `$68,000`.\n* **The Base-Load Tier:** Large tracked excavators (`Hydraulic Excavator, Track - 21.0 to 33.0 Metric Tons`) compose a predictable baseline price anchor between **$45,000 and $50,000**.\n* **Engineering Impact:** Standard ordinal label encoding would obscure these numeric step-changes. Because explicit performance capacities (Horsepower, Metric Tons) map monotonically to higher price valuations, incorporating **Target Encoding** or utilizing string parsing to extract physical integers from `FunctionalClassification` will yield highly predictive numeric features.\n","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"                                      \n# Plot 3.5: Manufacture Year Anomaly\n\nfig,axes = plt.subplots(1, 2, figsize=(14, 4))\nfig.suptitle('Plot 3.5: Manufacture Year Anomaly Detection',fontsize=14,fontweight='bold')\naxes[0].hist(train['ManufactureYear'],bins=80,color='steelblue',edgecolor='white')\naxes[0].axvline(1001,color='red',lw=2,ls='--',label=f\"Placeholder 1001:{(train['ManufactureYear']==1001).sum():,}rows\")\naxes[0].set_title(\"Raw Year Distribution (includes 1001)\")\naxes[0].legend()\n\nvalid_years = train[train['ManufactureYear']>1920]['ManufactureYear']\naxes[1].hist(valid_years,bins=60,color='seagreen',edgecolor='white')\naxes[1].set_title(\"Filtered Year Distribution (>1920)\")\naxes[1].set_xlabel(\"Year of Manufacture\")\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.show()","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-07-17T09:51:07.467504Z","iopub.execute_input":"20